WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:03.436
-The president
is arguing in court

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:05.271
that Congress
can't investigate him

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:08.007
as Republicans wage a war
on reproductive rights.

00:00:08.007 --> 00:00:10.410
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.611
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.913 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:16.749
-This week, it really
feels like we're seeing

00:00:16.749 --> 00:00:17.917
one threat after another

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:20.152
to our system
of Constitutional democracy.

00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:22.789
The president is vowing to block
all subpoenas from Congress,

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:24.323
his lawyers are arguing in court

00:00:24.323 --> 00:00:26.392
that Congress doesn't have
the power to investigate him,

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:28.895
the White House Counsel
told Congress this week

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:31.130
that Trump would refuse
all demands for records

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.765
and testimony related
to the Mueller report,

00:00:32.765 --> 00:00:34.634
and Trump is turning
the justice department

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:35.868
into a political weapon.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:37.937
At this point, the next
"National Treasure" movie

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:39.672
is just gonna be two hours of
Nick Cage

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.408
trying to tape the Constitution
back together.

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:44.777
[ As Cage ]
I'm still missing a piece!

00:00:44.777 --> 00:00:48.014
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:50.949
[ Normal voice ]
Earlier this week, for example,

00:00:50.949 --> 00:00:53.486
Trump said he would resist
all Congressional requests

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:55.254
for documents like
his tax returns

00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:56.723
because he thinks Congress

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.090
shouldn't be allowed
to see them.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:00:59.959
-Why continue to block
these House Democrats

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:01.026
who are looking for information?

00:01:01.026 --> 00:01:03.963
-Because they are asking
for things

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.631
that they're not entitled to.

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:08.301
I could ask them, I assume,
if they ask me,

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:09.803
I could ask them for
the same kind of thing.

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:10.937
They wouldn't want to do it.

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:12.271
-Yeah, they would.

00:01:12.271 --> 00:01:14.741
In fact, several Democratic
presidential candidates

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:16.809
have already released
their tax returns

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:18.744
because they have
nothing to hide.

00:01:18.744 --> 00:01:21.147
Do you think Elizabeth Warren
has a side hustle

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:23.249
selling hotels
to Russian mobsters?

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:24.684
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:27.020
At most, I can see her
running a B&amp;B

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:30.389
that serves breakfast
way too early.

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:32.058
"Be downstairs at 4:30

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:35.127
because the Cream of Wheat
goes fast!

00:01:35.127 --> 00:01:38.097
The Trump administration is even
refusing basic requests

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:40.833
for information about big banks
that have scammed customers.

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:44.303
Yesterday, for example,
Warren grilled Joseph Otting,

00:01:44.303 --> 00:01:47.340
the Comptroller of the Currency
during a Senate hearing.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.909
Now, the Office of the
Comptroller of the Currency,

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.844
or OCC, is charged in part with

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:53.512
regulating banks
like Wells Fargo.

00:01:53.512 --> 00:01:56.682
Warren asked Otting to release
information about the bank

00:01:56.682 --> 00:01:58.250
which has had a series
of scandals.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:59.518
Otting refused.

00:01:59.518 --> 00:02:01.720
Let's just say it did not
go well for him.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:04.624
-Will you commit to
publicly disclosing

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:08.027
the OCC's evaluation of the

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:12.664
"competence, experience,
character, or integrity,"

00:02:12.664 --> 00:02:15.034
of the next Wells CEO.

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.336
-I will not.

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:17.636
-Why not?

00:02:17.636 --> 00:02:19.805
-'Cause it'll be confidential
supervisory information.

00:02:19.805 --> 00:02:22.108
-It's confidential
if you make it confidential.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:23.509
The point is, you have
the legal authority --

00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:25.511
-At this point in time,
I do not have plans to release

00:02:25.511 --> 00:02:26.679
that information publicly.

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:28.748
-And what is the reason that you
don't have plans?

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:29.949
Why are you keeping this secret?

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:33.586
-As you indicated,
it's my prerogative.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:36.121
-Okay. And our job
is oversight here.

00:02:36.121 --> 00:02:38.191
-Senator Warren,
no one has been more tougher

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:39.858
on Wells Fargo than myself.

00:02:39.858 --> 00:02:41.127
No one has been more outspoken.

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:43.162
-You mean at the OCC?
That's a low bar.

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:44.564
-I would disagree with that.

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:46.499
I find it insulting that you
would make that comment.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:47.266
-Good.

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:48.467
-Oh!

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:50.502
What do you even say
in response to that?

00:02:50.502 --> 00:02:51.504
"I'm insulted."

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:54.440
"Good!
I'm glad you're insulted."

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:58.244
"Well, I'm glad...

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:00.813
that you're glad
that I'm insulted."

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:03.883
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.618
It's such a simple,
yet effective burn

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.419
that all you can do is
slink down in your chair

00:03:07.419 --> 00:03:09.422
and hope she forgets
you're there.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:11.323
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.323 --> 00:03:13.826
The president is arguing
that he can't be investigated

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:16.028
or subpoenaed,
and that Congress isn't entitled

00:03:16.028 --> 00:03:17.763
to information about him,
and then there's the fact

00:03:17.763 --> 00:03:20.099
that Republicans in Alabama
passed an inhumane

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:23.002
and blatantly unconstitutional
anti-abortion law

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.704
essentially inviting
the Supreme Court's

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:27.206
conservative majority
to overturn Roe v. Wade.

00:03:27.206 --> 00:03:28.741
If fact, last night,
the governor of Alabama

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.242
signed the bill into law
and actually admitted

00:03:30.242 --> 00:03:31.711
that it was unenforceable.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.613
-The most restrictive abortion
law in the nation

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:35.381
is now in effect in the state
of Alabama.

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:37.650
The governor of that state
signing the bill yesterday,

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:41.054
which bans all abortions unless
the mother's life is in danger.

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:42.922
Doctors in Alabama who perform
an abortion,

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:45.558
if convicted, would face
up to life in prison.

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:47.493
-Planned Parenthood and the ACLU

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.896
are challenging states who have
restricted abortion

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:51.597
saying lawmakers
are passing these bills

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:53.265
only to benefit their parties.

00:03:53.265 --> 00:03:55.701
-They know and say publicly
that these laws

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:58.705
are blatantly unconstitutional,
and they don't care.

00:03:58.705 --> 00:04:00.707
-Tonight, the governor here says

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:02.775
while she signed the abortion
bill,

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:05.845
she also knows
it is unenforceable

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:07.847
because of Roe v. Wade.

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:09.882
-Think about that.
They passed a bill

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.752
they know is unconstitutional,
and they don't care.

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:14.553
Can you imagine how Republicans
would react

00:04:14.553 --> 00:04:16.288
if New York and California
passed laws

00:04:16.288 --> 00:04:17.790
just banning all gun ownership?

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.058
The NRA would send out
an all caps e-mail,

00:04:20.058 --> 00:04:21.160
saying "Tyranny is here,"

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.695
Trump would tweet something
like,

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:24.097
"Gun grabbin' libs, not nice!"

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:25.898
with a bunch of weird
exclamation points,

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.666
and Sean Hannity
would scream so loud,

00:04:27.666 --> 00:04:29.201
the screen in your TV
would crack.

00:04:29.201 --> 00:04:32.572
Well, probably not your TV,
but your grandpa's TV.

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:33.806
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:35.141
And it will not
shock you to learn

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:37.009
that some of the men
voting for these bills

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:41.381
have absolutely no idea how
pregnancy or reproduction work.

00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:43.916
Take Republican state senator
Clyde Chambliss,

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:46.652
who was asked about the fact
that the bill does not provide

00:04:46.652 --> 00:04:49.321
exemptions in case
of rape and incest.

00:04:49.321 --> 00:04:51.758
Chambliss said that abortions
could only be provided

00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:54.627
until the woman
is known to be pregnant.

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:58.130
Okay. Already, what?

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:01.667
Is this some kind of ancient
Alabama riddle?

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:03.569
[ Southern accent ]
The buffet is all you can eat --

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:06.139
That is,
until you get to the restaurant.

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:10.175
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.175 --> 00:05:12.545
Chambliss also said...

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:15.014
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:17.316
He also said,
"I'm not trained medically,

00:05:17.316 --> 00:05:19.785
so I don't know
the proper medical terminology

00:05:19.785 --> 00:05:21.988
and time lines,
but from what I've read

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:24.823
and what I've been told,
there's some period of time

00:05:24.823 --> 00:05:27.226
before you can know
a woman is pregnant.

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:29.995
Wait.
You're not medically trained?

00:05:29.995 --> 00:05:32.632
Because...
you [bleep] nailed it, dude.

00:05:32.632 --> 00:05:37.002
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.002 --> 00:05:40.205
Did it really not ever
occur to you

00:05:40.205 --> 00:05:42.508
to look into the terminology
and the time lines

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:43.876
before voting on this bill?

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:45.878
It strikes me
the only time lines

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:48.014
these guys think they know
is you have sex,

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:51.517
and then nine months later,
a stork shows up.

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:53.085
In fact,
that comment was so dumb,

00:05:53.085 --> 00:05:55.688
Planned Parenthood actually
had to issue a fact check

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:56.989
on its Twitter account.

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:59.358
"When asked if this bill
makes an exception for victims

00:05:59.358 --> 00:06:01.327
of incest,
Senator Chambliss said,

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:03.029
'Yes, until she knows
she's pregnant.'

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:05.964
Again, that would mean that
that person would have to get

00:06:05.964 --> 00:06:08.100
an abortion before they know
they are pregnant.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:11.104
That's not a thing."

00:06:11.104 --> 00:06:12.438
It's not.

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:14.807
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:18.677
I mean...

00:06:18.677 --> 00:06:20.446
Who was this guy's
sex-ed teacher,

00:06:20.446 --> 00:06:23.482
a pole cat in a beer helmet?

00:06:23.482 --> 00:06:26.252
But, of course, this isn't about
protecting life.

00:06:26.252 --> 00:06:27.553
If that's what it was about,

00:06:27.553 --> 00:06:30.022
then Republicans would invest
money in maternity care,

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:32.958
parental leave, universal pre-K,
or any number of policies

00:06:32.958 --> 00:06:34.626
that would actually help
families raise children.

00:06:34.626 --> 00:06:36.195
What it's really about
is depriving women

00:06:36.195 --> 00:06:37.396
of their basic human rights.

00:06:37.396 --> 00:06:39.331
And Chambliss basically
gave the game away

00:06:39.331 --> 00:06:42.368
when he was asked why the bill
wouldn't apply to eggs

00:06:42.368 --> 00:06:44.203
fertilized through IVF.

00:06:44.203 --> 00:06:46.572
Chambliss said "The egg in the
lab doesn't apply.

00:06:46.572 --> 00:06:49.041
It's not in a woman.
She's not pregnant."

00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:50.375
Dude, you just admitted it --

00:06:50.375 --> 00:06:52.144
"It's not in a woman,
so we don't care."

00:06:52.144 --> 00:06:53.579
You said out loud

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:55.547
the thing Republicans
pretend they aren't doing.

00:06:55.547 --> 00:06:57.549
You're like one of those guys
selling fake watches

00:06:57.549 --> 00:06:59.752
on the street
and admitting it's fake.

00:06:59.752 --> 00:07:01.553
It's not a Rolex,
it's a Polex,

00:07:01.553 --> 00:07:02.921
and the numbers
are out of order.

00:07:02.921 --> 00:07:05.558
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:07.626
Now...

00:07:07.626 --> 00:07:10.629
these anti-abortion bills passed
by multiple states

00:07:10.629 --> 00:07:12.064
are blatantly unconstitutional.

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:15.434
In fact, the authors know
these bills will get overturned

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:17.036
in the lower courts.
That's the point.

00:07:17.036 --> 00:07:18.904
They want them to get
to the Supreme Court.

00:07:18.904 --> 00:07:20.706
And they're doing this now
because they think they've

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:23.309
finally got five conservative
justices on their side

00:07:23.309 --> 00:07:25.044
with the appointment
of Justice Brett Kavanaugh.

00:07:25.044 --> 00:07:26.678
You remember him,

00:07:26.678 --> 00:07:29.581
the bad guy from
every '80s teen movie.

00:07:29.581 --> 00:07:31.917
He looks like he should be
telling Michael J. Fox,

00:07:31.917 --> 00:07:34.754
"A werewolf can't play
basketball!"

00:07:34.754 --> 00:07:36.755
Of course, during
his confirmation process,

00:07:36.755 --> 00:07:38.690
Kavanaugh repeated
all the usual nonsense

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:41.360
about how he'd be a fair
and impartial judge.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:42.694
And honestly,
for the life of me,

00:07:42.694 --> 00:07:44.863
I just can't figure out
what would make Republicans

00:07:44.863 --> 00:07:46.331
think Kavanaugh
is on their side.

00:07:46.331 --> 00:07:48.901
He's always been pretty,
you know, balanced.

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:51.570
-Since my nomination in July,

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:54.473
there's been a frenzy
on the left

00:07:54.473 --> 00:07:55.841
to come up with something,

00:07:55.841 --> 00:07:59.211
anything to block
my confirmation.

00:07:59.211 --> 00:08:01.747
The behavior of several
of the Democratic members

00:08:01.747 --> 00:08:03.982
of this committee at my hearing
a few weeks ago

00:08:03.982 --> 00:08:05.718
was an embarrassment.

00:08:05.718 --> 00:08:09.021
This whole two-week effort
has been a calculated

00:08:09.021 --> 00:08:11.456
and orchestrated political hit,

00:08:11.456 --> 00:08:15.827
fueled with apparent pent-up
anger about President Trump

00:08:15.827 --> 00:08:18.531
and the 2016 election,

00:08:18.531 --> 00:08:21.734
revenge on behalf
of the Clintons,

00:08:21.734 --> 00:08:23.735
and millions of dollars in money

00:08:23.735 --> 00:08:28.574
from outside left-wing
opposition groups.

00:08:28.574 --> 00:08:30.977
This is a circus.

00:08:32.211 --> 00:08:34.779
[ Laughter ]

00:08:34.779 --> 00:08:35.914
-I mean, holy [bleep]

00:08:35.914 --> 00:08:37.749
That guy is a Supreme Court
justice now.

00:08:37.749 --> 00:08:39.318
Can you imagine
what his questions

00:08:39.318 --> 00:08:41.086
during oral arguments are like?

00:08:41.086 --> 00:08:44.523
"I saw Hillary Clinton
outside my house last night

00:08:44.523 --> 00:08:46.592
digging through my trash

00:08:46.592 --> 00:08:48.727
as part of
a left wing conspiracy

00:08:48.727 --> 00:08:52.431
to steal my identity
and make a mold of my face

00:08:52.431 --> 00:08:56.502
so she can wear it as a mask
and rob a liquor store."

00:08:56.502 --> 00:08:58.570
This guy accused...

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:02.008
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:02.008 --> 00:09:04.376
This guy accused the Clintons
of orchestrating

00:09:04.376 --> 00:09:07.145
a secret revenge plot with money
from left-wing opposition groups

00:09:07.145 --> 00:09:09.848
to destroy him, and now he could
be one of the deciding votes

00:09:09.848 --> 00:09:11.784
on everything from whether
Congress can investigate

00:09:11.784 --> 00:09:13.185
the president to Roe v. Wade.

00:09:13.185 --> 00:09:14.687
He sounds like he's auditioning

00:09:14.687 --> 00:09:16.822
for a talk show with Alex Jones.

00:09:16.822 --> 00:09:17.956
-They're demons.

00:09:17.956 --> 00:09:20.292
They're frickin'
interdimensional invaders, okay?

00:09:20.292 --> 00:09:23.829
I'll just say it. Make fun of me
all you want on CNN or wherever.

00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:25.664
But everyone already
innately knows this --

00:09:25.664 --> 00:09:28.768
These people are not frickin'
humans, okay?!

00:09:28.768 --> 00:09:31.703
Hillary Clinton
is a goddamn demon.

00:09:31.703 --> 00:09:34.039
Excuse me taking the Lord --
It's not taking it in vain.

00:09:34.039 --> 00:09:36.875
She is a demon damned to hell!

00:09:36.875 --> 00:09:38.511
Excuse me.

00:09:38.511 --> 00:09:39.644
[ Laughter ]

00:09:39.644 --> 00:09:42.615
-I like how he says "Excuse me"

00:09:42.615 --> 00:09:45.885
at the end like he just sneezed.

00:09:45.885 --> 00:09:49.921
For Alex Jones, an outburst
like that is just involuntary.

00:09:49.921 --> 00:09:51.690
[ As Jones ]
Joe Biden is a secret lizard

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:53.392
who smells like sulfur!

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:55.394
Gesundheit.

00:09:55.394 --> 00:09:56.628
[ Normal voice ]
Of course, throughout

00:09:56.628 --> 00:09:58.397
his confirmation process,
Kavanaugh repeated

00:09:58.397 --> 00:10:00.733
all the usual lines about
how he would supposedly respect

00:10:00.733 --> 00:10:02.968
Roe v. Wade as settled law.

00:10:02.968 --> 00:10:06.638
-Senator, I said
that it's settled as a precedent

00:10:06.638 --> 00:10:07.940
of the Supreme Court.

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:11.043
It has been reaffirmed
many times

00:10:11.043 --> 00:10:15.748
over the past 45 years,
as you know,

00:10:15.748 --> 00:10:20.085
and most prominently,
most importantly,

00:10:20.085 --> 00:10:24.523
reaffirmed in Planned Parenthood
versus Casey in 1992.

00:10:24.523 --> 00:10:28.026
I understand the importance
of the issue.

00:10:28.026 --> 00:10:32.598
I understand the importance
that people attach

00:10:32.598 --> 00:10:34.867
to the Roe v. Wade decision,

00:10:34.867 --> 00:10:38.370
to the Planned Parenthood versus
Casey decision.

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:40.372
I don't live in a bubble.

00:10:40.372 --> 00:10:42.007
I understand.

00:10:42.007 --> 00:10:43.642
I live in the real world.

00:10:43.642 --> 00:10:45.744
-Man, it's so weird to see
someone who's capable

00:10:45.744 --> 00:10:48.480
of losing his [bleep] like that
suddenly calm and measured.

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:51.150
It's like seeing a crazy guy
in the subway screaming,

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:53.219
"Rats controlled by the
government are spying on us!"

00:10:53.219 --> 00:10:54.386
And then he turns to you
and says,

00:10:54.386 --> 00:10:56.255
"By the way, that jacket
looks fantastic."

00:10:56.255 --> 00:10:58.223
[ Laughter ]

00:10:58.223 --> 00:11:00.726
Kavanaugh was lying about
Roe v. Wade,

00:11:00.726 --> 00:11:02.527
and we know he was lying
because he said

00:11:02.527 --> 00:11:04.697
the exact opposite in an e-mail

00:11:04.697 --> 00:11:06.065
when he worked for
the Bush administration.

00:11:06.065 --> 00:11:07.733
-Somebody leaked
to "The New York Times"

00:11:07.733 --> 00:11:10.469
and then to NBC News this e-mail

00:11:10.469 --> 00:11:12.437
written by Brett Kavanaugh
in 2003

00:11:12.437 --> 00:11:15.641
in which he argues explicitly
that Roe versus Wade

00:11:15.641 --> 00:11:18.310
is not recognized to be
settled law

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:21.880
because the Supreme Court
could very well overturn it.

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:24.583
"I am not sure that all legal
scholars refer to Roe

00:11:24.583 --> 00:11:27.486
as the settled law of the land
at the Supreme Court level

00:11:27.486 --> 00:11:30.823
since Court can overrule
its precedent.

00:11:30.823 --> 00:11:33.124
And three current justices
on the Court would do so.

00:11:33.124 --> 00:11:34.292
-Man, I'd love to hear

00:11:34.292 --> 00:11:36.061
Kavanaugh's explanation
for that.

00:11:36.061 --> 00:11:38.396
[ As Kavanaugh ] Hillary Clinton
snuck into my office

00:11:38.396 --> 00:11:41.567
wearing a mask of my face
and typed that on my computer

00:11:41.567 --> 00:11:42.701
to frame me!

00:11:42.701 --> 00:11:46.404
And Alex Jones is right,
she's a demon from hell!

00:11:46.404 --> 00:11:49.274
Excuse me.

00:11:49.274 --> 00:11:52.545
[ Normal voice ] Our system
of Constitutional democracy

00:11:52.545 --> 00:11:54.479
facing one threat after another.

00:11:54.479 --> 00:11:56.615
Congress should be able to
investigate the president.

00:11:56.615 --> 00:11:58.984
Women should be able to make
choices about their own bodies.

00:11:58.984 --> 00:12:00.385
I can't believe
I have to say that,

00:12:00.385 --> 00:12:02.821
and if you're offended by me...
-Good.

00:12:02.821 --> 00:12:04.523
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:04.523 --> 00:12:05.924
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:05.924 --> 00:12:08.394 line:0%
♪♪

